{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>In the place where the burnt offering is slaughtered shall the sin offering be slaughtered.</b> The commentators said that this is in order to cover over the sinners, for people will say that he is bringing an עֹלָה. But this reasoning is weak, for in any case his iniquity is revealed when they see that he does not offer it whole as a burnt offering. And furthermore, the עֹלָה is a male and the חַטָּאת is a female. Now concerning the matter of the עֹלָה, there are those who say that it comes for the contemplation of transgression, and there are those who say that the עֹלָה is among those offerings that are offered without iniquity (Psalms 51:18). And for those who say that there is in the עֹלָה an aspect of atonement for sin, the reason for the matter is that the heart, which is placed on the left side, is the cause of all sin, for the heart desires and the instruments of action complete — therefore the slaughter of both of them is in the north, to indicate that the heart has perverted him (Isaiah 44:20), and out of the north the evil opens (Jeremiah 1:14). And for those who say that the עֹלָה comes only as a gift, their proof being from what is written (Psalms 66:13) 'I will come to Your house with burnt offerings' — we may say that the sinner, after he has set his heart to return in repentance and to bring a חַטָּאת for atonement, from that moment onward he is accepted and his offering is accepted before HaShem, blessed be He, as though he had offered an עֹלָה, the most exalted of all the offerings."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:35:24.546451604Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}